<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea Shipping - Steel scrap cargoes - July 2.</title>
<headline>S.Korea Shipping - Steel scrap cargoes - July 2.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is the arrival schedule for major steel scrap vessels unloading at South Korean ports of Inchon, Pusan, Masan, Pohang, Kwangyang and Asan, as detailed on Wednesday by South Korean surveyors.</p>
<p>Steel scrap cargoes</p>
<p>-- INCHON PORT</p>
<p> VESSEL	    TONNE    ETA	 ETD	  BUYER</p>
<p> Canavera	  40,000   July 5		   Inchon</p>
<p> Feng Shou	 50,000   July 15		  Inchon</p>
<p> Rova		38,391   End of July	    Inchon</p>
<p>-- PUSAN PORT</p>
<p> Delta-Trident   35,000   Jun 14    July 2     Dongkuk</p>
<p>-- MASAN PORT</p>
<p> Yunling	   22,793   July 1    July 12    KISCO</p>
<p>-- POHANG PORT</p>
<p> Fivi		26,110   June 27   July 10    Kangwon</p>
<p> Delta Peace     48,000   July 4    July 31    Kangwon</p>
<p> Qupa		22,500   July 8    July 28    POSCO</p>
<p> Caspian-Trident 38,000   July 22		  POSCO</p>
<p> Seabee 1	  42,000   July 26		  POSCO</p>
<p>-- KWANGYANG PORT</p>
<p> Faethon	   30,000   July 1    July 10    POSCO</p>
<p> Kupa		22,000   July 10		  POSCO</p>
<p> Feng Yao	  50,000   July 10		  POSCO</p>
<p> Al Qawiyyu	30,000   July 16		  POSCO</p>
<p> Lok Kranti	31,000   July 24		  POSCO</p>
<p> Xing Su Hai     30,000   Aug  2		   POSCO</p>
<p>-- ASAN PORT</p>
<p> Cenk-Kaptanoglu 31,407   June 19   July 1     Hanbo</p>
